  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Paracel: Sustainable Forestry and Competitive Infrastructure Financing</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Paracel S.A. (&#x201c;Paracel,&#x201d; the &#x201c;Company,&#x201d; or the &#x201c;Client&#x201d;) is developing a large-scale pulp project in Concepci&#xf3;n and Amambay, Paraguay, which includes the construction of an industrial plant for bleached eucalyptus Kraft pulp, with an annual production capacity of 1.8 million tons, a forestry program covering 203,000 hectares, and various complementary civil works, (i.e., power lines, substations, port, and access roads) the &#x201c;Pulp Project&#x201d;.The Pulp Project was approved by IDB Invest in 2022, and since then, Paracel has been complying with the requirements established in both IDB Invest&#x2019;s Environmental and Social Sustainability Policy and the Environmental and Social Action Plan agreed upon by the parties.</narrative>
  </description>
